# Docker matches a slash-less pattern only at the context root, so the entries that must hold at
# any depth are `**/`-prefixed: a bare `coverage` or `.claude` would let a nested one into the
# image. That is how apps/backend/.env used to get in while .gitignore hid it from `git status`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.git
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
**/.playwright-mcp
**/.codegraph
**/.claude
**/*.test.ts
**/*.typecheck.ts
# Root-anchored on purpose (#877): no process in a container reads them, and a commit that changes
# only these must not invalidate `COPY . .` (the CI compose job checks the layers). The files a
# container does read are listed in docs/deploy.md -> Files a package reads; none is here
# (tooling/image.test.ts D1). The drizzle snapshots are drizzle-kit's, never the migrator's.
docs
audits.md
README.md
.github
deploy
packages/db/drizzle/meta/*_snapshot.json
